<Component>
    <Description>
        IF[language]EQUAL_TO"de"THEN Eine Sicherung. Nicht ruecksetzbar.
        Der gegebene Wert ist der Wert des Stromes in Ampere, bei welcher die Sicherung ausloest.        
        Idealisiertes modell is unabhaengig von der Temperatur und hat keine Zeitverzoegerung (ausser der Zeitverzoegerung durch die Berechnung, welche i.d.R. sehr klein ist).
        ELSE A Fuse. Not resettable.
        The value given is the current value in Ampere, at which this fuse interrupts.
        Idealized model is independent of temperature and has no time delay (except the time step of calculation, which usually is very small).
        ENDIF
    </Description>
    <purchase>
        <link>
            <url>www.conrad.com/p/mta-blade-fuse-839701</url>
            <title>IF[language]EQUAL_TO"de"THEN"Flachsicherung"ELSE"Blade fuse"ENDIF</title>
            <detail>IF[language]EQUAL_TO"de"THEN"Flachsicherung mit max 7.5A bei Conrad Electronic. Andere Ampere-Werte auswaehlbar."ELSE"Blade fuse with max 7.5A at conrad electronic. Other Ampere values can be selected."</detail>
        </link>
        <link>
            <url>www.conrad.com/c/fuses-c17392</url>
            <title>IF[language]EQUAL_TO"de"THEN"Uebersicht"ELSE"Overview"ENDIF</title>
            <detail>IF[language]EQUAL_TO"de"THEN"Uebersicht Sicherungen und Zubehoer bei Conrad Electronic"ELSE"Overview of Fuses at Conrad Electronic"ENDIF</detail>
        </link>
    </purchase>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Device:Fuse
    </eeschema_sch>
    <eeschema_sch>
       L Device:Fuse_Small
    </eeschema_sch>
        <purchase>
		<link>
			<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fsicherungen-17392.html</url>
			<title>Overview of fuses</title>
			<detail>Overview of fuses at conrad electronic<detail>
		</link>
      </purchase>
		
    <Spice>
        DEFINE [max_amp] AS_NUMBER OF:[value]
      IF[max_amp]THENELSE
        DEFINE [max_amp]    AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:imax IN:[value]
        DEFINE [time_irupt] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:time IN:[value]
        DEFINE [i2t]        AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:i2t  IN:[value]
        IF [max_amp]    THEN DEFINE [max_amp]    AS_NUMBER OF:[max_amp]    ENDIF
        IF [time_irupt] THEN DEFINE [time_irupt] AS_NUMBER OF:[time_irupt] ENDIF
        IF [i2t]        THEN DEFINE [i2t]        AS_NUMBER OF:[i2t]        ENDIF
      ENDIF
        IF [max_amp] THEN
            IF [max_amp] HIGHER_THAN 0 THENELSE
                <Dialog type="warning" title="Please enter a correct value for [name]">The value of fuse [name] at position  ([xpos] | [ypos]) should be higher than 0, but is [max_amp]</Dialog>
            ENDIF
        ELSE
            <Dialog type="error" title="Please enter a correct value for [name]"> Missing threshold current value for fuse [name] at position ([xpos] | [ypos]): Please give that fuse a numeric value. That value will be the current in Ampere, at which the fuse interrupts.
            
            Alterntively, you can define the maximal current value in ampere (imax) and either the time delay to interrupt(time) or the i2t value (i2t), separated by spaces, for example:
            imax=5 time=2e-3 
            (Here the maximal current is 5A and the maximal overcurrent time is 2x10⁻³s=2ms. 
            That overtime does not reset, but "heals" gradually in the times where there is no overcurrent)
            other example:
            imax=2.3 i2t=0.2
            (Here the maximal current is 2.3A and the i2t=0.2A²s, but be aware that the use of i2t is nonlinear and is known to cause exceptions in some circuit simulations in ngspice.)
            </Dialog> 
        ENDIF
      //Model:
      .subckt fuse_[name] pa pb 
      .param tau=0.63
      .model si1 sw ron=1E9 roff=0.5 vt=tau //ron=resistance AFTER the fuse interrupts in Ohm. roff=resistance BEFORE the fuse interrupts in Ohm
      //switch to turn off current
      s1 pa pb moff 0 si1 
      
      IF [i2t] IS_NUMBER && [i2t] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
        R_time mpre moff 1
        C_time moff 0 [i2t]
        //                |<-- hold -->|         |<------- set ------->|  
        BVS_fuse mpre 0 V=V(moff) >= tau ? 0.64 : abs(I(s1)) > [max_amp] ? (abs(I(s1))-[max_amp])**2 : 0
        
      ELSEIF [time_irupt] IS_NUMBER && [time_irupt] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
        R_time mpre moff 1
        C_time moff 0 [time_irupt]
        //                |<------- set ------->| || |<-- hold -->|
        BVS_fuse mpre 0 V=(abs(I(s1)) > [max_amp] || V(moff) > tau) ? 1 : 0
      ELSE
        //                |<------- set ------->| || |<-- hold -->|
        BVS_fuse moff 0 V=(abs(I(s1)) > [max_amp] || V(moff) > tau) ? 1 : 0
      ENDIF ENDIF
      .ends
      //Component   
      X_[name] [pin1] [pin2] fuse_[name]
    </Spice>
    <eeschema_symbol>
		IF [model] ENDS_WITH Small THEN
			DRAW
			S -50 20 50 -20 0 1 0 N
			P 2 0 1 0 -50 0 50 0 N
			X ~ 1 -100 0 50 R 50 50 1 1 P
			X ~ 2 100 0 50 L 50 50 1 1 P
			ENDDRAW
		ELSE
			DRAW
			S -30 -100 30 100 0 1 10 N
			P 2 0 1 0 0 100 0 -100 N
			X ~ 1 0 150 50 D 50 50 1 1 P
			X ~ 2 0 -150 50 U 50 50 1 1 P
			ENDDRAW
		ENDIF
    </eeschema_symbol>
</Component>

<Component>
    <Description>
        (EN)A Fuse. Resettable.
        The value given is the current value in Ampere, at which this fuse interrupts.
        Resets itself, when the voltage drop over this fuse is smaller than or equal to v_reset.
        Idealized model is independent of temperature and has no time delay (except the time step of calculation, which usually is very small).
    
        (DE)Eine Sicherung. Ruecksetzbar.
        Der gegebene Wert ist der Wert des Stromes in Ampere, bei welcher die Sicherung ausloest.        
        Setzt sich zurueck, wenn der Spannungsabfall ueber dieser Sicherung geringer oder gleich v_reset ist.
        Idealisiertes modell ist unabhaengig von der Temperatur und hat keine Zeitverzoegerung (ausser der Zeitverzoegerung durch die Berechnung, welche i.d.R. sehr klein ist).
    </Description>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Device:Polyfuse
    </eeschema_sch>
    <eeschema_sch>
       L Device:Polyfuse_Small  
    </eeschema_sch>
     <purchase>
		<link>
			<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fsicherungen-17392.html</url>
			<title>Overview of fuses</title>
			<detail>Overview of fuses at conrad electronic<detail>
		</link>
      </purchase>
      <Default_Values>
          imax=8.5A vreset=3250mV Ron=1E9 Ohm Roff=0.5Ohm
      </Default_Values>
    <Spice>
      IF IS_NUMBER [value] THEN
        DEFINE [max_amp] [value]
        
        DEFINE [v_reset] 0.1
        DEFINE [Ron] 1M  // = 1E9
        DEFINE [Roff] 0.1
      ELSE
        DEFINE [max_amp] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:imax=IN:[value]
        DEFINE [max_amp] AS_NUMBER OF:[max_amp]
        
        DEFINE [v_reset] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:vreset=IN:[value]
        DEFINE [v_reset] AS_NUMBER OF:[v_reset]
        
        DEFINE [Ron] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:Ron IN:[value]
        DEFINE [Ron] AS_NUMBER OF:[Ron]
        
        DEFINE [Roff] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:Roff IN:[value]
        DEFINE [Roff] AS_NUMBER OF:[Roff]
      ENDIF
      IF [max_amp] && [v_reset] && [Ron] && [Roff] THENELSE
        <Dialog type="error" title="Please enter a correct value"> 
            Missing interrupt current value for polyfuse [name] at position ([xpos] | [ypos]):
            you can either just enter a number in ampere, for example:
            8.5
            (Here the interrupt current is 8.5A, and the reset voltage has the default value of 0.1V) 
            
            or you can write the maximal ampere and the reset voltage, for example:
            imax=16 vreset=3250m Ron=1E9 Roff=0.5
            (Here the interrupt current is 16A, and the reset voltage is 3250mV=3.250V)
        </Dialog>
      ENDIF
      
      //Model:
      .subckt fuse_[name] pa pb 
      .param v_reset=IF[v_reset]THEN[v_reset]ELSE0.1ENDIF //fuse resets when voltage drop over this component in V <= v_reset
      .model si1 sw vt=0.5 ron=[Ron] roff=[Roff]  //ron=resistance AFTER the fuse interrupts in Ohm. roff=resistance BEFORE the fuse interrupts in Ohm
      
      //switch to turn off current
      s1 pa pb m1 0 si1 
      //                  |<---- set --------->| || (|<-hold-->| && |<------not reset------->|)
      BVS_polyfuse m1 0 V=abs(I(s1)) > [max_amp] || (V(m1) > 0.5 && abs(V(pa)-V(pb)) > v_reset) ? 1 : 0
      .ends
      //Component   
      X_[name] [pin1] [pin2] fuse_[name]
    </Spice>
    <eeschema_symbol>
		IF [model] ENDS_WITH Small THEN
			DRAW
			S -20 50 20 -50 0 1 0 N
			P 2 0 1 0 0 100 0 -100 N
			P 4 0 1 0 -40 50 -40 30 40 -30 40 -50 N
			X ~ 1 0 100 25 D 50 50 1 1 P
			X ~ 2 0 -100 25 U 50 50 1 1 P
			ENDDRAW
		ELSE
			DRAW
			S -30 100 30 -100 0 1 10 N
			P 2 0 1 0 0 100 0 -100 N
			P 4 0 1 0 -60 100 -60 60 60 -60 60 -100 N
			X ~ 1 0 150 50 D 50 50 1 1 P
			X ~ 2 0 -150 50 U 50 50 1 1 P
			ENDDRAW
		ENDIF
    </eeschema_symbol>
</Component>
<Component>
    <Description>
        An antenna with one pin. If a numeric value is given, then the maximal amplitude of the antennas signal is that value in volts. If no value is given, then the maximal amplitude is 1 Volt.
        The Voltage of this one-pin-antenna is created from ground node to the one pin. So this antenna contains a finite "isolation resistance" to ground.
        
        This model consists of four voltage sources, which generate a voltage which looks like noise in a transient analysis, and a resistor to simulate a finite resistance to ground. Might match well to some antennas in some surrounding circuits, but there will definitely be some other cases where this model does not fit well. A model of white noise would fit better to a real antenna, however we were not able to create a working white noise model in the spice section. The user can get something that looks similar to white noise in a transient analysis by setting the parameter "base_time" to a value similar to the timestep of the simulation (which is already set by default).
    </Description>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Device:Antenna
    </eeschema_sch>
    <Default_Values>
        100mV // amplitude of the antenna signal
    </Default_Values>
    <Spice>
     .subckt device_antenna_1pin_[name] pin
     //independen parameters: relatively easy to change them correctly
     .param base_time=[timestep] // for the frequencies of the noise
     .param isolation_ohms=1E6
     
     .param amplitude=IF[value] IS_NUMBER THEN[value]ELSE1ENDIF //maximal voltage amplitude, in positive and negative direction
     
     //dependent parameters: change these only if you know what you do:
     .param frq1=1/base_time
     .param frq2=sqrt(3)/base_time
     .param frq3=sqrt(5)/base_time
     .param frq4=sqrt(7)/base_time
     .param vi=amplitude/4
     R_isolation 0 1 isolation_ohms
     V1 1 2   sin(0 vi frq1)
     V2 2 3   sin(0 vi frq2)
     V3 3 4   sin(0 vi frq3)
     V4 4 pin sin(0 vi frq4)
    .ends
    X_[name] [A] device_antenna_1pin_[name]
    </Spice>
    <eeschema_symbol>
    (symbol "Antenna_0_1"
      (polyline
        (pts
          (xy 0 2.54)
          (xy 0 -3.81)
        )
        (stroke (width 0.254) (type default))
        (fill (type none))
      )
      (polyline
        (pts
          (xy 1.27 2.54)
          (xy 0 -2.54)
          (xy -1.27 2.54)
        )
        (stroke (width 0.254) (type default))
        (fill (type none))
      )
    )
(symbol "Antenna_1_1"
      (pin input line (at 0 -5.08 90) (length 2.54)
        (name "A" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
        (number "1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
      )
    )

    </eeschema_symbol>
</Component>

<Component>
    <Description>
        An antenna with one pin and a shield. If a numeric value is given, then the maximal amplitude of the antennas signal is that value in volts. If no value is given, then the maximal amplitude is 1 Volt.
        The Voltage of this pin-antenna is created from ground node to the pin [A]. So this antenna contains a finite "isolation resistance" to ground.
        
        The shield's electrical model consists of a resistance and a capacitance.
        The antenna's model consists of four voltage sources, which generate a noise, and a resistor to simulate a finite resistance to ground. Might match well to some antennas in some surrounding circuits, but there will definitely be some other cases where this model does not fit well. A model of white noise would fit better to a real antenna, however we were not able to create a working white noise model in the spice section. The user can get something roughly similar to white noise by setting the parameter "base_time" to a value similar to the timestep of the simulation (which is already set by default).
        
        The Antenna might also be printed on a PCB, a chip. Here the chip is seen as a shield for that antenna. Therefor the model Device:Antenna_Chip is included here too.
    </Description>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Device:Antenna_Shield
    </eeschema_sch>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Device:Antenna_Chip
    </eeschema_sch>
    <Default_Values>
        100mV 	
    </Default_Values>
